# End Of Day Review

## Core Instruction
Close the day by converting completed visible work into progress, reconciling canonical state in `ACTION_LEDGER` and `DECISION_QUEUE`, refreshing the human-readable backlog, and briefing {{USER_NAME}} on what happened, what remains, and what needs a decision.

## Default Workflow
1. Read:
   - [[vault/Operations/ACTION_LEDGER.md]]
   - [[vault/Operations/DECISION_QUEUE.md]]
   - [[vault/Backlog.md]]
   - [[vault/Notes and Journal.md]]
   - [[vault/Operations/OPERATOR_LOG.md]]
   - [[vault/Operations/OPERATOR_HANDOFF.md]]
   - [[vault/Operations/LOG.md]]
2. Determine the current local date and time from the `Timezone:` value in `[[vault/Operations/SCHEDULE.md]]`; if it is missing, fall back to `America/Los_Angeles`.
3. Inspect today's `Today` section and today's Journal entry.
4. Reconcile today's visible checklist against canonical evidence before harvesting:
   - keep unchecked items open when the source of truth still shows prepared, waiting, or unresolved state
   - mark unchecked items complete when `ACTION_LEDGER`, `LOG`, or another authoritative local source clearly proves the item was completed under a different shape
   - do not infer completion from intent, partial prep, or Chronicle/Codex-session candidates alone
5. Convert every checked `- [x]` item in today's `Today` section into today's `**Progress:**` block unless an equivalent entry already exists.
   - use concise active-outcome wording
   - remove scheduling qualifiers like "today" when they are not part of the outcome
   - do not log unchecked items
6. {{USER_NAME}} matching `ACTION_LEDGER` items `done` when the completed item maps clearly.
7. Reconcile canonical state:
   - remove completed work from active daily rendering by setting it `done`
   - keep external waiting states as `waiting`
   - keep unresolved questions in `DECISION_QUEUE`
   - if a decision was answered in chat or visible note state, mark it resolved
   - if a decision is stale or low-confidence, apply its reprompt policy instead of carrying it forever
8. Review Operator log/handoff items from today:
   - reconcile completed Operator work into canonical state when proof is clear
   - include user-visible Operator completions in the EOD brief when they matter
   - do not log Operator's internal work as {{USER_NAME}}'s `**Progress:**`
9. Refresh `[[vault/Backlog.md]]` from reconciled canonical state so completed Today items do not remain visible as backlog.
10. Preserve the human note:
   - keep previous Journal days intact
   - update only today's `**Progress:**`, `Snapshot`, and small daily view when needed
   - do not recreate the old heavy operational lanes
11. Refresh `last_updated` in changed routed docs.
12. Post the EOD brief.

## Rules
- Do not fabricate progress from intent alone.
- Do not ignore checked `Today` items; checked items are completion evidence unless contradicted by context.
- Do not leave a daily checkbox open when stronger local evidence clearly proves the work was completed.
- Do not copy unfinished `Today` items into a new dated section.
- Do not leave completed work active in `ACTION_LEDGER`.
- Do not let decisions vanish without being resolved, dismissed, or reprompted according to policy.
- Do not put machine-state complexity back into `Notes and Journal`.
- Do use `[[vault/Backlog.md]]` for backlog visibility instead of putting backlog into the daily note.
- Do not create a separate project-planning layer inside LifeOps; projects are only domain context unless {{USER_NAME}} explicitly adopts a project-management tool.
- Do not log {{COS_NAME}}'s internal work in `**Progress:**`; log only {{USER_NAME}}'s completed actions.
- Do not include passive happenings as progress just because they appeared in a source log.
- Do not rewrite {{USER_NAME}}'s freeform Journal notes.
- Do not skip the end-of-day brief just because there are no blockers.
- Do not invent open questions when none exist.
- Do not treat Operator logs as {{USER_NAME}}'s personal progress; they are execution outcomes to reconcile and brief when useful.

## Exception Rule
If expected sections are missing, repair the minimum structure needed for the EOD pass and log the repair in `LOG.md`.

## Output Contract
- Update `[[vault/Operations/ACTION_LEDGER.md]]` and `[[vault/Operations/DECISION_QUEUE.md]]` when state changed.
- Refresh `[[vault/Backlog.md]]` when backlog visibility changes.
- Update `[[vault/Notes and Journal.md]]` only as the lightweight human surface.
- Post a concise EOD brief with:
  - what happened today
  - what still needs attention
  - open questions, if any
